Point Features. To encode the quad layout effectively, each input point is equipped with the following feature signals:
- (1) Point position 𝒑 and normal 𝒏;
- (2) 𝒅𝑑𝑐 (𝒑) , 𝒅 𝑐 (𝒑), and the unit surface gradients of both fields, i.e . , ∇𝒅𝑑𝑐 (𝒑)− (∇𝒅𝑑𝑐 (𝒑)·𝒏)𝒏 ∥∇𝒅𝑑𝑐 (𝒑)− (∇𝒅𝑑𝑐 (𝒑)·𝒏)𝒏∥ and ∇𝒅 𝑐 (𝒑)− (∇𝒅 𝑐 (𝒑)·𝒏)𝒏 ∥∇𝒅 𝑐 (𝒑)− (∇𝒅 𝑐 (𝒑)·𝒏)𝒏∥ ;
- (3) Offset vectors from 𝒑 to the centers of the chart and dual chart where 𝒑 resides.
Here, although DCDF or CDF alone can characterize the quad layout alone, due to surface sampling and VAE capacity, we find that including both fields, as well as their gradients and offset vectors, helps improve layout learning and the later layout extraction process.
